-**Theorem** (root: any carrier, reading and requirement, the requirement supplied and fixed before the outcome; no premise and no choice). *A response common over a reading.* The occurrences at which a given region holds throughout their closure under a relation form the largest region inside it closed under the relation (`«所闭之承最大»`); at a process's steps it is the viability kernel (`Viability.kernel_iff_held`), whose two laws are proved from it. A judgment through the couplings is a common response over the class alike through them ([§3](#r-testing-within-couplings)): one region for each act, inside that act's requirement and closed under the reading, the regions covering the situations. For every reading and requirement such a response exists exactly where every situation has an act whose requirement holds throughout its closure under the reading (`«共应当且仅当所闭之承遍»`): the acts' kernels cover the situations, the reading standing where a process's steps stand, so judgment is viability indexed by acts. Where the reading is a map's sameness and the requirement gives exactly one act at each situation, a common response exists exactly where the image of the response relation along the map has a fixed successor (`«遍定应共应当且仅当像定后»`), the lumping law on a carrier keeping situations and acts apart. A rule from what a map reads gives one with no choice (`«依读而应则共应»`). A rule from a common response asks for one act chosen for each reading, which [§9](#r-when-to-inquire-and-when-to-respond)'s uniform policy has with choice over the readings as a hypothesis; that such choice cannot be dropped is shown for plans ([§9](#r-finite-continuation-plans)), not for this rule. Witnesses show that the closure, covering, one act and the sum carrier each do work, and that an act at every situation, or one shared by every two, need not give one: under the reading that tells nothing apart they give none (`«共应之例»`) ([record](../results/records/a-response-common-over-a-reading.md)).
